  "id": "DrugBank_DB02362 - MONDO_6361",
  "verbalization": "Aminobenzoic Acid is implicated in the pathogenesis of Penile Fibromatosis through a shared pathway involving Collagenase Clostridium Histolyticum. The evidence suggests that Aminobenzoic Acid may act as a mediator in the development of Penile Fibromatosis by influencing the expression or activity of Collagenase Clostridium Histolyticum, which is associated with multiple conditions, including Balanitis Xerotica Obliterans and Peyronie Disease. This connection implies a potential role for Aminobenzoic Acid in modulating the inflammatory or fibrotic processes that underlie Penile Fibromatosis. The overlapping indications with Collagenase Clostridium Histolyticum suggest a possible mechanism where Aminobenzoic Acid may influence the degradation of collagen or other extracellular matrix components, contributing to the fibrotic changes observed in Penile Fibromatosis. While the exact mechanism remains unclear, the integrated evidence points to a potential link between Aminobenzoic Acid and Penile Fibromatosis through its interaction with Collagenase Clostridium Histolyticum, highlighting a broader role in inflammatory and fibrotic disease processes.",
